 {"id": "PERF-002", "title": "P1 recall does TWO full read_json scans of the namespace on every call (queryMemories + countMemories each re-ingest all chunk files) — single-scan variant with COUNT(*) OVER () is 2.3x faster at scale", "priority": "P1", "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-09-26", "created_by": "perf", "complexity": 2, "detail": "Evidence (duckbrain-perf tick 2026-09-26-15-27-09, warm numbers, prod-scale namespaces on disk):\ncommand:  hyperfine --warmup 2 --runs 10 'node bin/duckbrain.js recall --namespace coding-hermes --limit 5'\n  before:  4.591s +- 1.258s (min 3.588 max 7.629) [User 3.197s System 1.602s]; hermes-memory ns: 1.048s +- 0.025s\n  live daemon: GET /api/memories?limit=5&namespace=coding-hermes over unix socket = 3.79-3.89s (warm, 3 runs); hermes-memory = 0.26-0.35s\nprofile:  node --cpu-prof on coding-hermes recall: 71.4% (idle) = blocked on disk I/O; readdir 10.1%; strace: 475k stat/access syscalls (237,667 newfstatat + 238,023 access) per call — read_json mounts EVERY chunk file per scan\nisolated DuckDB bench (same engine, same file list, tsx script vs :memory:):\n  coding-hermes (19,811 files, 133MB jsonl): two-scan page+count = 1078+904 = 1982ms; ONE-scan (COUNT(*) OVER () window in the page query) = 857ms -> 2.3x, IDENTICAL rows (5) and total (245,208)\n  hermes-memory (757 files): 116ms -> 48ms (2.4x), identical results\nhot path: recallTool always runs BOTH legs at src/mcp/tools/recall.ts:983-986 (queryMemories then countMemories; retry block lines 994-995 too); each of src/duckdb/queries.ts queryMemories (~line 412) and countMemories (~line 560) independently calls collectJsonlFiles + read_json over the full chunk list; countMemories exists to satisfy GAP-024 'total = unlimited match count'\nchange: fuse the two scans into one SQL pass: SELECT *, COUNT(*) OVER () AS __total FROM (<dedup inner>) WHERE __rn=1 AND action!='tombstone' ORDER BY ... LIMIT n; read total from the first row's __total (or MAX(__total) when the page is empty — emit one extra probe row or run the count only when the page returns 0 rows). Keep the GAP-024 contract: total must stay the unlimited match count.\nexpected effect: warm daemon list latency on the fleet's biggest namespace ~3.9s -> ~2.6s (count scan removed), CLI recall ~4.6s -> ~3.3s; larger effect after follow-up materialization of dedup state. NOTE the remaining ~2.6s is read_json re-ingest itself (724ms single count at SQL level vs 2.9-3.9s through the tool path — the gap is worth a second row once this lands).\nACCEPTANCE: (a) repro: recall ?limit=5 on namespaces/coding-hermes returns identical memories AND identical total before/after; (b) exactly ONE read_json reference per list request in DuckDB query logs or code path; (c) empty-page case (offset beyond end) still reports the true total; (d) bench command above re-run: coding-hermes warm daemon < 3.0s.", "closed_at": "2026-09-30T04:50:00-05:00", "close_reason": "stale-resolved: PERF-003 fused single-scan landed (commit 0b5be05); board row was not flipped in tick 617"}
