ded INFO OOM on the SAME red suite (rc=1 from EACCES), so both cells carried no repo signal this cycle — attribute their outcomes to this defect, not as independent findings.", "review_notes": "Evidence: agent native.log tail — Test Files 9 failed | 169 passed (178), Tests 41 failed | 1373 passed (1414 collected); 8x EACCES on /tmp/.duckbrain-write/test-memory-ZA0dJ8.lock, 8x test-memory-timerange-csQPJ7.lock, 8x test-memory-attr-1w8a9J.lock, 6x test-memory-recency-AWkROT.lock; ls -ld /tmp/.duckbrain-write = drwxrwxr-x 1004:1004 (agent uid 1021). Failing files: src/duckdb/queries-timerange-retr003.test.ts, src/duckdb/queries.test.ts, src/duckdb/queries-attr-retr006.test.ts, src/duckdb/queries-recency-retr005.test.ts, src/git/asof-ddl-compat.test.ts, src/git/autocommit-ops006-drain.test.ts, src/git/autocommit-ops006.test.ts, src/git/autocommit.test.ts, src/cli/unix-socket-flag.test.ts. Repro on any multi-uid box: create /tmp/.duckbrain-write owned by another uid, run pnpm test:run — every insertMemory-through-serializer test fails EACCES. Code path: src/serialization/lock.ts namespaceWriteLockPath joins .duckbrain-write under the RESOLVED namespaces root; for the legacy test-partition arm (src/duckdb/queries.ts resolveSerializationTarget) that root is path.dirname(resolvedPartition) — but the observed paths show the lock dir resolving to the SHARED /tmp/.duckbrain-write (uid-1004-owned, created Sep 22 by another tenant), i.e. the fixed-name dir is cross-uid shared by design. Dev-box green run: pnpm test:run at HEAD a9f84bb (pristine git-archive checkout, /home/kara/qa-duckbrain-head) — 178/178 files, 1412/1412 tests, rc=0.", "blocks": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "worker_status": "complete", "dispatched_at": null, "completed_at": "2026-09-30T00:30:00Z", "attempts": 1, "exit_code": null, "commit_hash": "a6df7ca", "files_changed": null, "lines_added": 0, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": "QA tick 02b798f post-merge battery 188/188 files 15