 {"id": "AUTH-DEFAULT-001", "title": "P1 — The open-write default was closed at the DEPLOYMENT layer twice, never in code: cli/http.ts authType still defaults to \"none\" on BOTH main and feat/native-s3, and package.json start:http passes no --auth, so a fresh installer following the README gets an unauthenticated write endpoint.", "priority": "P1", "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-09-27T16:14:38.590891+00:00", "created_by": null, "complexity": 2, "detail": {"fingerprint": "72883ef13d1e6bc6552feeb6401e755dc1ff7e124bd5442c6df5c7a6b8c975d6"}, "reasoning": "Third-party review (carterlasalle method), clean clone of main @ 42cea0a, scratch daemon :3997. REPRO: `node bin/duckbrain.js http --port 3997` (exactly what package.json start:http does, minus the port) then `curl -X POST localhost:3997/api/memories -d '{\"key\":\"/x\",\"domain\":\"raw_note\",\"content\":\"nope\",\"namespace\":\"review\"}'` -> HTTP 201; the row lands on disk and the audit ledger records `principal: null`. The same write against `--auth=apikey` -> 401 with a `denials.jsonl` entry. SOURCE OF TRUTH: feat/native-s3 src/cli/http.ts:403 `...(options.authConfig ?? { type: options.authType ?? \"none\" })`; main @ 42cea0a src/cli/http.ts:396 carries the identical expression. git log -S on that expression returns ONE commit (13b9090, a prettier reformat) — it has never been flipped. package.json start:http = `node bin/duckbrain.js http --port 3000`, unchanged on both branches. WHY THIS IS NOT A DUPLICATE: DB-GAP-031 is marked complete with commit_hash describing a HOST-LEVEL flip (systemd drop-ins dbgap031-auth.conf, 5 consumer scripts, minted tokens) and its own note says 'Ops flip (no worker)'; DF-0924-07 is marked complete but its worker_summary states verbatim 'Default (no flag/env) unchanged' — it only made --auth-file/DUCKBRAIN_AUTH_FILE auto-enable apikey. So the class reads complete twice while the code default and the documented front door remain open. The fleet's own :3000 is protected by deployment; a new installer is not. FIX DIRECTION: flip the code default to apikey (or bind 127.0.0.1-only unless auth is explicitly enabled) so the safe posture is the default and local dev opts out loudly. 1-2h including test + README updates. EVIDENCE LEVEL: measured live (fresh clone, scratch port 3997/3998); footer commit 42cea0a, Node v22.22.3, pnpm 12.4.2, 2026-09-27.", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T21:43:55Z", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-09-27 21:43:55.000000", "commit_hash": "22e2b7a", "files_changed": ["src/cli/http.ts", "src/cli/http-auth.test.ts", "bin/duckbrain.ts", "README.md", "docs/api/http-api.md", "docs/guide/getting-started.md", "AGENTS.md"], "lines_added": 150, "lines_removed": 40, "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "pushed, CI pending", "worker_summary": "Foreman-direct after first worker dispatch stalled with zero diff. createHttpServer default authType none->apikey; 26 hermetic test seams made explicit; 3 regression tests (keyless 401 + no row, valid key 201, --auth=none 201); help/docs default flip; AGENTS.md 179/1427.", "foreman_note": "Live proof on scratch daemon :3699: keyless write 401 with zero rows on disk, valid key 201, --auth=none keyless 201. Verdict dfe96ea1 FAIL = stale-diff artifact of killed first attempt; post-hoc tier1-only ddd13c7e after async tier2 wedge.", "attempts": 1, "dispatched_at": "2026-09-27T21:43:55Z"}
 {"id": "RATE-LIMIT-001", "title": "P1 — Default HTTP rate limit is 100 req/min and 429s are NEVER logged: a bulk ingest loses ~78% of writes while the daemon log shows nothing wrong. cli/http.ts:391 `requestsPerMinute: options.rateLimit ?? 100`.", "priority": "P1", "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-09-27T16:14:38.590891+00:00", "created_by": null, "complexity": 2, "detail": {"fingerprint": "03074e21c5d3143ae70175c9818ea6a6779672c319a97d68c37f7868e634ad50"}, "reasoning": "Third-party review (carterlasalle method), clean clone of main @ 42cea0a, scratch daemons :3997 (default) and :3996 (--rate-limit 6000). MEASURED at the default: 500 sequential authenticated writes -> accepted=111, refused=389 all HTTP 429 with `Retry-After: 1`; only 29 of the 100 intended distinct keys ever landed. Response headers confirm the bucket: `X-RateLimit-Limit: 100`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0`. MEASURED at --rate-limit 6000 on the SAME build: 300 sequential -> 300/300 in 2.83s (106 writes/s); 200 concurrent with 32 workers -> 200/200 in 0.67s (299 writes/s); write latency mean 9.9ms / median 9.4ms / p95 13.0ms / max 15.7ms; 651 rows on disk, 0 unparseable. So the ENGINE is not the constraint at this scale — the default limiter is, and raising it is a config change, not a code change. TWO DEFECTS, one row: (a) 100 req/min per bucket is the wrong shape for the stated multi-agent use case, and because the localhost/tailnet side door arrives as 127.0.0.1 the whole co-located fleet shares ONE bucket rather than getting one each; (b) 429 refusals appear nowhere in the daemon log, so an operator watching logs sees a healthy server while writes silently vanish from the caller's perspective. Log limit/remaining/retry-after at WARN regardless of what the limit becomes (~1h). No existing board row covers either half (grep for ratelimit/429 found only incidental matches: a CI flake title, PUSH-001's per-namespace autopush interval, and DB-SUPA-3's route listing). EVIDENCE LEVEL: measured live; footer commit 42cea0a, Node v22.22.3, pnpm 12.4.2, 2026-09-27, ports 3996/3997.", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T16:14:38.590891+00:00", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-09-27T22:15:01Z", "commit_hash": "85ab900", "files_changed": ["src/auth/ratelimit.ts", "src/auth/ratelimit.test.ts"], "lines_added": 134, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "RED — run 36354878908 exact HEAD d16a531 failed only AGENTS.md count assertion (live 179 suites/1430 tests); count follow-up filed", "worker_summary": "Worker rework committed 85ab900: every 429 emits JSON console.warn with event, IP, limit, remaining=0, retryAfter; 3 regression tests; focused 9/9, tsc clean, prettier clean.", "foreman_note": "Implementation commit 85ab900 + GitReins evidence commit d16a531 pushed; verdict b1753722 passed. CI count drift is a separate follow-up: /tmp/rate-limit-001-agents-edit.md records the sanctioned AGENTS.md correction and exact red step. Default 100 req/min was not changed; this tick landed the silent-429 observability half.", "attempts": 2, "dispatched_at": "2026-09-27T21:43:55Z"}
