 {"id": "SUPA6-DECLARE-GAP-001", "title": "P2 — DB-SUPA-6 (declared DDL surface) is marked complete, but on a fresh install there is NO discoverable way to declare a table: the per-namespace OpenAPI spec returns paths: 0 and no CLI or HTTP declare verb was found.", "priority": "P2", "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-27T16:14:38.590891+00:00", "created_by": null, "complexity": 3, "detail": {"fingerprint": "08cad1141de2d694e16083779b581c9dcfb286356a75954e7824a6151c1f31d5"}, "reasoning": "Third-party review (carterlasalle method), clean clone of main @ 42cea0a, authed scratch daemon :3995. OBSERVED: GET /api/ns/review/openapi.json -> 200, valid OpenAPI doc, `paths: 0`, with info.description stating it is 'Generated from the declared table registry (namespaces/<ns>/tables/*.table.json). PostgREST-style filters/order/paging on every table.' A fresh namespace dir contains only .git, _audit/, manifest.json, raw_note/ — no tables/ dir, so the empty spec is internally consistent. The gap is discoverability: `duckbrain help` exposes remember/recall/namespace/squash/query and NO tables verb (grep for declare|create|add under src/cli/ found nothing); POST /api/ns/review/tables -> 404 because the mount is relative (POST /:table inserts a ROW into an existing table, it does not declare one). So the declared-table REST layer is unreachable from a fresh install by any documented path, even though SUPA-6, DOC-5 and DB-SUPA-3 all read complete. MY WRONG GUESS, RECORDED: I assumed POST /api/ns/<ns>/tables declared a table; it does not. FIX DIRECTION: ship one example .table.json in the scaffold and/or a `duckbrain tables declare` verb so the spec is self-teaching (0.5-1d). VERIFY: a declaration path may exist somewhere I did not search — confirm before dispatching. EVIDENCE LEVEL: measured live (:3995) + grep over src/ at 42cea0a.", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T16:14:38.590891+00:00"}
 {"id": "PERF-003", "priority": "P1", "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-09-27", "created_by": "perf", "complexity": 2, "title": "P1 recall fuses the count leg into the page scan: COUNT(*) OVER () on the DEDUPED set kills the second full read_json — 1.36x live CLI, 2.05-3.0x at SQL layer, identical rows+total", "reasoning": "Re-validation of PERF-002 on tick duckbrain-perf-2026-09-27-15-50-05 (fresh measurements, same input scale: namespaces/coding-hermes, 19,826 jsonl chunk files, ~245k live rows; node-duckdb 1.4; box loadavg 53-67 during A/B — both arms suffered it equally).\nREPRO (exact command, paired A/B via env toggle, same build = tsx dev-on-the-fly, same warm conditions):\n  hyperfine --warmup 2 --runs 15 'DUCKBRAIN_PERF2_FUSED=0 node bin/duckbrain.js recall --namespace coding-hermes --limit 5' 'DUCKBRAIN_PERF2_FUSED=1 node bin/duckbrain.js recall --namespace coding-hermes --limit 5'\n  before (legacy two-scan): 5.169s +- 0.615s [User 3.677s Sys 1.763s] min 4.067 max 6.224, 15 runs\n  after  (fused one-scan):  3.793s +- 0.666s [User 2.941s Sys 1.170s] min 2.982 max 5.464, 15 runs  -> 1.36x faster, no range overlap\n  (uncontended earlier baseline this tick, legacy shape: 4.450s +- 0.607s — matches PERF-002's 4.591s; loadavg contamination explained the higher absolute arms)\nISOLATED SQL BENCH (same engine, same file list, /tmp/perf002-revalidate2.js vs :memory:):\n  two-scan page+count = 3491+4604 = 8095ms; fused one-scan = 3950ms -> 2.05x; IDENTICAL 5 page rows and IDENTICAL total 245,328\n  first-shape check: COUNT(*) OVER () placed on the RAW scan gives total 246,075 (pre-dedup) and BREAKS the GAP-024 contract — the window MUST sit outside the dedup WHERE (this was caught and corrected in this probe; the row's original sketch is ambiguous on this point)\n  naive-shape bench (/tmp/perf002-revalidate.js, window pre-dedup): 10,205ms two-scan vs 3,407ms fused = 3.00x — even faster but WRONG total, do not ship that shape\nCORRECTNESS EVIDENCE: `node bin/duckbrain.js recall --namespace coding-hermes --limit 5` before vs after: all 10 output records identical byte-for-content and in order (jq deep-compare: memories equal=True, ids equal in order=True); __total served from the fused window satisfies GAP-024 (unlimited match count) because the window is evaluated on the deduped set BEFORE LIMIT/OFFSET — the empty-page case (offset beyond end) still carries a row-level __total, verified by SQL semantics (window computed pre-LIMIT); full GAP-024 empty-page test pass belongs to the foreman's run\nhot path: src/mcp/tools/recall.ts:983-986 still calls queryMemories then countMemories back-to-back (same file, retry block 994-995); src/duckdb/queries.ts queryMemories SQL (~line 467) and countMemories (~line 570) each mount ALL chunk files via read_json — the fused query returns __total alongside the page\nprobe implementation (REVERTED after measurement — foreman implements for real): a DUCKBRAIN_PERF2_FUSED env toggle in src/duckdb/queries.ts, fused shape = SELECT *, COUNT(*) OVER () AS __total FROM (dedup inner) WHERE __rn=1 AND action!='tombstone', countMemories short-circuits to the captured total; module-level capture var is a thread-safety/abstraction smell to redesign in the real fix (e.g. recall.ts calls a combined query+total API instead of two functions)\nexpected effect: warm daemon list latency on the fleet's biggest namespace ~5.3s -> ~3.9s (CLI-equivalent ratio; daemon GET /api/memories?limit=5&namespace=coding-hermes measured 5.301s +- 1.437s warm this tick, 15 runs, same namespace), CLI 5.2s -> 3.8s under load, better when the box is quiet; the remaining ~3.8s is read_json re-ingest itself (~600-800ms at SQL level) — the tool-path gap is a second, separate finding (PERF-002's NOTE stands)\nACCEPTANCE: (a) repro command above shows FUSED=1 arm faster with non-overlapping ranges; (b) recall output identical (rows AND total) before/after, including empty-page offset case; (c) exactly ONE read_json per list request; (d) GAP-024 total = unlimited deduped match count (NOT the raw scan count — see the 246,075 trap above); (e) `pnpm vitest run tests/` green on the foreman's implementation.", "completed_at": "2026-09-29T03:55:00-05:00", "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "0b5be05", "worker_summary": "glm-5.3-flash@zai-glm worker: queryMemoriesWithTotal() combined API (dedup-window COUNT(*) OVER () pre-LIMIT), recall.ts hot path + retry block converted; countMemories retained for other callers", "files_changed": "src/duckdb/queries.ts, src/mcp/tools/recall.ts, src/duckdb/queries-fused-total-perf003.test.ts (new, 233L), AGENTS.md count sync", "lines_added": 448, "lines_removed": 34, "guard_result": "gitreins tier2 judge 7cb5897e PASS (tier1 passed; verdict COMPLETE); suite 183/184 pass 1464/1464 (gap046 config-ordering flake greens solo), tsc clean, prettier clean", "foreman_note": "AGENTS.md counts 183/1458 -> 184/1464 synced foreman-direct via sanctioned toggle (restored true); full-suite gap046 failure = config-ordering contamination, solo green, pre-existing class", "ci_result": "CI success on work commit 0b5be05 and closeout e1fd937 (batched, both green)"}
